mixin () {
  /// Static Markdown description of this canister's public API, authored from
  /// the current backend source. Reads no state.
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# SELLER_NET_WATERFALL backend API\n\nThis canister persists immutable snapshot run records for the SELLER_NET_WATERFALL\nseller net sheet calculator. It performs **no financial computation**: the\ncanonical calculator runs in the frontend as a pure module, and the backend\nstores the submitted snapshot verbatim and returns it unchanged. Snapshots are\nopaque JSON strings — the backend never parses, recomputes, or alters financial\nvalues.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\nEvery run-record method is scoped to the caller's principal.\n\n- `saveRunRecord` and `deleteRunRecord` require a **signed-in (non-anonymous)**\n  caller. An anonymous caller receives `#err(#notAuthenticated)`.\n- `listRunRecords` and `getRunRecord` are queries. An anonymous caller receives\n  an empty list (`[]`) or `null` respectively; they never trap.\n- `getApiDoc` is a public query and requires no authentication.\n\nThe app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at\n`/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the\nuser's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal\nagainst that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`).\nSuch a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it\nexpires.\n\nThere is no registration prerequisite for run records: any signed-in principal\nmay save and read its own records. The first caller to `_initialize_access_control`\nreceives the `#admin` role; subsequent callers receive `#user`. Run-record\nendpoints do not consult roles — they are scoped purely by principal identity.\n\n## Methods\n\n### `saveRunRecord(input : SaveRunRecordInput) : async Result<RunRecordView, RunRecordError>`\n\nPersists one snapshot for the caller. `input` carries:\n\n- `runId : Text` — client-generated identifier, unique per owner.\n- `calculatorVersion : Text` — version of the canonical calculator that produced\n  the snapshot.\n- `propertyId : Text` — property / case identifier supplied by the user.\n- `effectiveInputsJson : Text` — the effective inputs the calculator actually\n  used, serialized as JSON.\n- `inputProvenanceJson : Text` — per-field provenance state, serialized as JSON.\n- `inputHash : Text` — deterministic hash of the effective inputs.\n- `outputsJson : Text` — calculator outputs, serialized as JSON.\n\nThe backend assigns `createdAt` itself (nanoseconds since the Unix epoch) and\nreturns the stored record. `runId`, `calculatorVersion`, `inputHash`,\n`effectiveInputsJson`, and `outputsJson` must be non-empty; otherwise the call\nreturns `#err(#invalidInput(message))`.\n\n**Retry safety.** Saving is not idempotent: a second `saveRunRecord` with the\nsame `runId` for the same owner returns `#err(#alreadyExists(runId))` and does\nnot overwrite the stored snapshot. A retried call after a timeout therefore\neither succeeds once or reports `#alreadyExists`; it never duplicates or\nmutates a record. To replace a snapshot, delete it first.\n\n### `listRunRecords() : async [RunRecordView]`\n\nReturns the caller's records, newest first by `createdAt`. Anonymous callers\nreceive `[]`.\n\n### `getRunRecord(runId : Text) : async ?RunRecordView`\n\nReturns the caller's record with that `runId`, or `null` when it does not exist\nor the caller is anonymous. Records are owner-scoped: a caller can never read\nanother principal's record.\n\n### `deleteRunRecord(runId : Text) : async Result<(), RunRecordError>`\n\nDestructively removes the caller's record. Returns `#ok(())` on success,\n`#err(#notFound(runId))` when no such record exists for the caller, and\n`#err(#notAuthenticated)` for an anonymous caller. Deleting an already-deleted\nrecord returns `#notFound`; the operation is safe to retry.\n\n### `getApiDoc() : async Text`\n\nReturns this document.\n\n## Errors\n\n`RunRecordError` is a variant:\n\n- `#notFound : Text` — no record with this `runId` exists for the caller.\n- `#alreadyExists : Text` — a record with this `runId` already exists for the\n  caller.\n- `#notAuthenticated` — the caller is anonymous.\n- `#invalidInput : Text` — the submitted snapshot failed a structural check.\n\n## Units and encoding\n\n- `createdAt` is an `Int` in **nanoseconds** since the Unix epoch.\n- `owner` is a `Principal`.\n- All JSON payload fields are `Text` and are stored and returned **verbatim**;\n  the backend does not validate their internal structure beyond non-emptiness.\n- Money and rates live inside the JSON payloads and are never interpreted here.\n\n## Data-intelligence access (OQL)\n\nThe persisted run records are exposed to the platform's data-intelligence layer\nas the `runRecord` entity, flattened from the nested owner → runId → record\nstore into one row per record with an `owner` column. The entity is\n`controllerOnly`: only the platform controller (the data-intelligence agent)\nreads it, and it is not readable by end users through `execute`/`schema`. The\nJSON payload columns are opaque text.\n\n## Gotchas\n\n- Snapshots are **opaque JSON stored verbatim and never recomputed**. The\n  backend cannot repair or re-derive a snapshot; replay determinism depends on\n  the frontend calculator version recorded in `calculatorVersion`.\n- `saveRunRecord` is create-only. There is no update endpoint.\n- `listRunRecords` and `getRunRecord` are queries and may be served from a\n  replica that lags the latest update; poll after a save if strict read-your-write\n  ordering is required.\n- Anonymous callers never trap on reads; they receive empty results.\n"
  };
};
